  "result": "Perfect! All 142 tests pass. I've successfully added customer statements functionality:\n\n**New `statement()` in `src/statements.js`:**\n- Generates a customer statement showing outstanding invoices\n- Takes `customerId`, array of `invoices`, and `asOf` date (YYYY-MM-DD)\n- Returns `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })`\n\n**Statement includes:**\n- Only invoices with status 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (excludes draft and paid)\n- Only invoices with issueDate on or before `asOf` cutoff\n- For each invoice: `{ number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due }`\n  - `total` from `invoiceTotals()`\n  - `due` from `balanceDue()` (amount still owed)\n- Invoices sorted by issueDate (earliest first)\n- `totalDue` = sum of all due amounts\n\n**Error handling:**\n- Returns CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND for unknown customers\n\n**Features:**\n- Normalizes customer ID (handles case/whitespace)\n- Includes partially paid invoices (showing remaining balance)\n- Excludes paid invoices entirely (status no longer 'issued' or 'partially_paid')\n- Respects date filtering (only shows invoices issued before cutoff)\n\n**Tests added (12 new):**\n- Basic statement generation\n- Customer ID filtering and normalization\n- Status filtering (includes issued/partially_paid, excludes draft/paid)\n- Date filtering by issueDate\n- Sorting by issueDate\n- Total due calculations\n- Error handling for unknown customers\n- Verification that dueDate and total are correctly included\n\nThe statement system provides a complete account summary for any customer, showing all outstanding invoices and their individual balances.",
